    "subjectId": "gk-culture",
    "title": "Handicrafts & Geographical Indication (GI) Clusters of UP: Moradabad, Firozabad, Bhadohi, Kannauj",
    "subtitle": "One District One Product (ODOP), Peetal Nagari, Suhag Nagari, Attar City & Terracotta of Gorakhpur",
    "learningObjective": "Master the prominent handicraft and industrial craft clusters of Uttar Pradesh under the One District One Product (ODOP) and GI framework.",
    "introduction": "Uttar Pradesh leads all Indian states in the number of Geographical Indication (GI) tagged products (exceeding 69 registered products in 2024). Through its pioneering <strong>One District One Product (ODOP)</strong> scheme initiated in 2018, UP revitalized traditional artisan clusters that have operated for centuries: Moradabad ('Peetal Nagari'), Firozabad ('Suhag Nagari'), Kannauj ('Attar City'), Saharanpur, and Gorakhpur.",
    "detailedExplanation": "<h3>1. Major Artisan Craft Capitals of Uttar Pradesh</h3>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Moradabad \u2013 Brassware ('Peetal Nagari', GI Tagged):</strong> Global hub for handcrafted brass artware, engraved planters, lamps, and metal idols, utilizing Sand Casting and intricate engraving (<em>Naqqashi</em>).</li>\n  <li><strong>Firozabad \u2013 Glassware & Bangles ('Suhag Nagari' / Glass City):</strong> Centuries-old center for mouth-blown and furnace-manufactured glass bangles, chandeliers (Jhumars), glassware, and crystal artifacts.</li>\n  <li><strong>Kannauj \u2013 Traditional Perfume ('Attar / Ittar City', GI Tagged):</strong> World capital of natural essential oils and perfumes; utilizes ancient hydro-distillation in copper stills (<em>Deg-Bhapka</em> method) using sandalwood base oil. Renowned for <em>Mitti Attar</em> (distilling the scent of parched earth after the first rain).</li>\n  <li><strong>Gorakhpur \u2013 Terracotta ('Gorakhpur Terracotta', GI Tagged):</strong> Traditional red clay pottery and baked animal figurines (elephants, horses, Ganesha, chandeliers) crafted by rural potters without modern molds, using natural colors.</li>\n  <li><strong>Saharanpur \u2013 Wood Carving (GI Tagged):</strong> Renowned for delicate openwork fretwork and relief carving in Sheesham, Teak, and Mango wood.</li>\n  <li><strong>Khurja \u2013 Ceramic Pottery (Bulandshahr, GI Tagged):</strong> Famous for hand-painted glazed ceramic pottery, artistic tableware, and floral tiles.</li>\n  <li><strong>Aligarh \u2013 Locks & Hardware (GI Tagged):</strong> Celebrated as 'Tala Nagari' for handcrafted brass, iron, and lever padlocks.</li>\n  <li><strong>Mirzapur \u2013 Brass & Bell Metal Utensils (GI Tagged):</strong> Traditional casting of bronze and brass domestic utensils.</li>\n  <li><strong>Nizamabad \u2013 Black Clay Pottery (Azamgarh, GI Tagged):</strong> Unique black earthenware fired in an oxygen-deprived kiln and inlaid with silver-zinc powder designs.</li>\n</ul>",
